cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ANIMA in your work, please cite it as follows."
title: "ANIMA: A Developmental Spiking Neural Organism that Forages"
abstract: >-
  ANIMA is a self-organizing spiking neural organism, written from scratch in Rust, that lives in a
  3D world, senses its surroundings, controls its body, and forages for food. It uses no
  hand-designed internal architecture, no pretrained models, and no external memory modules. This
  release documents the demonstrated forager, the measured selective-learning wall, and the
  measured evolutionary fitness wall, all reproducible from a deterministic frozen identity line.
